It seems that in order to achieve my goal, I have to use middleware to achieve the desired results.

```
export default defineNuxtRouteMiddleware((to, from) => {
  const keepArray = [
    [ "/","/:column(3d|su|cz|tt|dg|ps|cad)/:id(\\d+).html" ],
    [ "/anli", "/anli/:id.html"],
    [ "/lg", "/lg/:id.html" ]
  ]
  const fromPath = from.fullPath;
  const toPath = to.fullPath;
  const fromMatchedPath = from.matched.length > 0 ? from.matched[0].path : "";
  const toMatchedPath = to.matched.length > 0 ? to.matched[0].path : "";
  const keep = keepArray.find(x=> x.includes(toPath) || x.includes(toMatchedPath));
  if(keep)
  {
    to.meta.keepalive = true;
    if(!(fromPath === toPath ||
        (keep.includes(fromPath) && keep.includes(toMatchedPath)) ||
        (keep.includes(toPath) && keep.includes(fromMatchedPath))
    )){
      from.meta.keepalive = false;
    }
  }
  else {
    from.meta.keepalive = false;
    to.meta.keepalive = false;
  }
}
```

You can use a routing middleware to do this, such as using useState to record a list, and each time you compare whether it is in the list, you can set the page you want to go to as keepalive. This example is not perfect, however, because of a bug built into nuxt3 that causes the keepalives to change for all pages every time you set any to.meta.keepalive to true.
```
export default defineNuxtRouteMiddleware((to,from)=>{
    if(useAliveList().value.indexOf(to.path)>=0){
        to.meta.keepalive=true;
    }else{
        to.meta.keepalive=false;
    }
    useAliveList('add',to.path);
});
```

